WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:01.463
<v Instructor>So the question is,</v>

2
00:00:01.463 --> 00:00:02.580
how do you make your connection

3
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:05.460
between data center and AWS redundant?

4
00:00:05.460 --> 00:00:07.140
So for this, we can use, for example,

5
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:10.290
in terms of VPN connections, an active-active setup.

6
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:11.123
So as we can see,

7
00:00:11.123 --> 00:00:13.290
we have two Corporate Data Centers, 1 and 2,

8
00:00:13.290 --> 00:00:14.340
and they're both connected

9
00:00:14.340 --> 00:00:18.180
through a dedicated VPN connection into AWS.

10
00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:19.980
Now what happens that also your Corporate Data Centers

11
00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.390
and Corporate Data Center 1 and 2,

12
00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:22.560
they are connected with each other

13
00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.480
with an internal connectivity.

14
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.490
So what happens that if, for example,

15
00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.770
this first VPN connection goes down,

16
00:00:28.770 --> 00:00:32.400
then your network can root from Corporate Data Center 1

17
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.130
to Corporate Data Center 2 into AWS,

18
00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.710
thanks to this redundant active-active VPN connection

19
00:00:37.710 --> 00:00:39.993
and vice versa if this connection is down.

20
00:00:40.950 --> 00:00:43.230
This happens as well when you use Direct Connect.

21
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.510
So you have two Direct Connect connections

22
00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:47.130
on two Corporate Data Centers,

23
00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:50.730
and then these are connected through internal networking.

24
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.020
And therefore, if one of these

25
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.610
Direct Connect location goes down,

26
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:55.050
then one Corporate Data Center

27
00:00:55.050 --> 00:00:59.730
can still access AWS through the other data center location.

28
00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.250
And then finally, if you wanted to mix them up together,

29
00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:04.650
you could of course choose a hybrid backup VPN location.

30
00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.900
For example, here your Corporate Data Centers

31
00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.770
are connected with each other,

32
00:01:07.770 --> 00:01:11.640
as well as with a rest through a VPN and a Direct Connect.

33
00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.710
And so if one of these things even failed,

34
00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:15.600
then you have a failover route

35
00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.280
through Corporate Data Center 1

36
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:19.500
or Corporate Data Center 2.

37
00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:21.150
Also, another feature you need to know about

38
00:01:21.150 --> 00:01:24.210
is that the Direct Connect Gateway SiteLink feature,

39
00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:25.320
which allows you to send data

40
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:27.660
from one Direct Connect location to another

41
00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.030
bypassing the AWS regions.

42
00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:30.990
So how does that work?

43
00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:33.540
Well, with this, you can create a private network connection

44
00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:35.430
between your on-premises data centers

45
00:01:35.430 --> 00:01:38.640
by connecting them directly to Direct Connect location,

46
00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.250
and the data will be sent over the fastest path

47
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.870
within these Direct Connect locations.

48
00:01:42.870 --> 00:01:46.290
So we have two Corporate Data Centers and they have routers

49
00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:47.880
and they're in different locations,

50
00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:49.470
so around the world of course.

51
00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:52.260
So we connect them to different Direct Connect locations

52
00:01:52.260 --> 00:01:54.090
around the world as well.

53
00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:59.010
And on the side of AWS, we create a Direct Connect Gateway.

54
00:01:59.010 --> 00:02:02.190
What's going to happen is that if we do enable SiteLink,

55
00:02:02.190 --> 00:02:04.440
then this kind of traffic can happen

56
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.150
where the Corporate Data Center

57
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:08.730
goes for Direct Connect to the Gateway

58
00:02:08.730 --> 00:02:11.910
back to another Direct Connect to the customer router,

59
00:02:11.910 --> 00:02:15.480
and this happens to connect the Corporate Data Center A

60
00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.910
with Corporate Data Center B

61
00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:21.360
without being routed through the AWS regions.

62
00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.670
So, that's called Site SiteLink. Okay?

63
00:02:23.670 --> 00:02:24.660
So that's it for this lecture.

64
00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:27.660
I hope you liked it, and I will see you in the next lecture.

